GCP (Google Cloud storage).

What is cloud storage
GCS= Google managed object storage  for any amount of unstructured data , access over HTTPS APIs.

Application → Bucket  → Object.

Backups , static websites , data lakes , Media , ML dataset . Terraform state.

Bucket and objects.
BUCKET : Name is globally unique.
Has Location , default  storage class , IAM
Live inside a Project

OBJECTS:
Data + metadata , up to 5 TB.
Name up to 1024 bytes
Immutable : an update creates a new generation.
Has generation number.

Location
Choose were data lives. It cannot be changed after the bucket created

Region:
One region Asia-south1
Lowest cost
Best when  compute is in same region

Dual-Region (DR)
Two specific Region
Higher availability
Turbo replication option (15 min RPO)

Multi-Region (MR)
Large area US, EU , Asia
Higher availability
Good for Global content serving(CDN   means cloud Front)


RPO = Recovery Point Objective : How much recent data could you lose in a disaster.
Storage Classes
1. Standard     Day: None        Frequent
2. Nearline     Day: 30 days    about once a month
3. Cold line    Day: 90 days    about once a quarter
4. Archive      Day: 365 days  about once a year 

Early deletion fee : Deleting or overwriting before the minimum duration still charges the remaining days.

Default class is set on the bucket ,. You can also set the class per object

Lifecycle and Auto class.
Lifecycle rule :  
Condition: Age , created before , storage class , number of newer version
Action: Delete , SetStorageClass , Abort Incomplete Multiple Upload


AUTOCLASS:  Bucket Setting .  Moves object between class automatically based on access pattern , without you writing rules , check current pricing for management fees.

Security : Access Control
Prefer IAM(Identity Access Management) , ACLs (Access Control lists).
 
